  "notes": "ちゃんと is a colloquial adverb meaning \"properly\" or \"correctly.\" Very common in everyday speech.\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Properly, correctly (doing something the right way)\n2. Reliably, without fail (dependably)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ちゃんと{食|た}べる: to eat properly\n- ちゃんと{聞|き}く: to listen properly\n- ちゃんと{来|く}る: to come without fail\n- ちゃんとした: proper, decent (modifies nouns)\n\nSIMILAR ADVERBS:\n- きちんと: properly, neatly (slightly more formal)\n- しっかり: firmly, thoroughly\n- きっちり: precisely, exactly\n\nREGISTER:\nColloquial. Often used by parents speaking to children, but common among all ages in casual speech.\n\nEXAMPLE CONTEXTS:\n- ちゃんとした{服|ふく}: proper clothes\n- ちゃんとした{仕事|しごと}: a proper job\n- ちゃんとした{大人|おとな}: a responsible adult",
